WEBVTT

00:36.911 --> 00:38.162
Hey. Kim.

00:38.246 --> 00:39.789
EPISODE 7

00:39.872 --> 00:42.833
Geez. Is this your first day in business?
Don't worry about it.

00:42.917 --> 00:44.669
- Just buy me a drink--
- Hey, boys!

00:47.004 --> 00:48.047
Wait, hold on.

00:48.756 --> 00:50.633
- What the hell?
- I don't have much time.

00:50.716 --> 00:52.677
So I'll keep it short.

00:52.760 --> 00:56.180
There's an important shipment coming in
from China tomorrow night, right?

00:56.264 --> 00:59.100
We need to make some adjustments
to those goods.

00:59.225 --> 01:02.853
So, we need to borrow your little shop
for just two days.

01:02.937 --> 01:06.691
Think of it as a location sponsorship.

01:06.774 --> 01:07.984
What the hell?

01:08.067 --> 01:11.988
What are these assholes on about?

01:12.071 --> 01:14.323
Hey, what are you doing? Get 'em!

01:19.245 --> 01:20.746
What are you waiting for? Go ahead.

01:20.830 --> 01:22.665
- By myself? What about you?
- You scared?

01:22.748 --> 01:24.417
Scared? Hell no.

02:18.638 --> 02:19.639
I'll kill them.

02:34.070 --> 02:35.071
What the hell?

02:51.003 --> 02:52.004
So what's it going to be?

02:52.546 --> 02:53.547
Can we borrow it?

02:58.636 --> 03:00.721
- Ow, my back.
- Geez, it's so dusty.

03:00.805 --> 03:03.849
You should've helped sooner
instead of trying to look cool.

03:04.517 --> 03:08.229
- There were only like seven guys.
- I had them, but you jumped in.

03:08.312 --> 03:10.064
You would've been dead without me.

03:10.147 --> 03:11.941
You would have been dead
if it weren't for me.

03:13.943 --> 03:16.779
Hey, Seong-won. Location secured.

03:16.862 --> 03:19.281
Now let's get set up. Yeah.

03:21.450 --> 03:24.120
- Hey, you're so dusty.
- Stop it!

03:26.706 --> 03:29.041
We'll be working together from now on.

03:29.125 --> 03:30.543
So I'll speak casually.

03:30.626 --> 03:33.713
- Is that okay?
- Yes, whatever works for you.

03:33.796 --> 03:35.089
I like your attitude.

03:36.006 --> 03:37.007
First things first.

03:37.800 --> 03:39.176
I need you to operate this.

03:41.637 --> 03:42.638
This thing?

03:42.722 --> 03:44.974
Yeah, why? It's small.
Doesn't look too difficult.

03:47.643 --> 03:49.979
So, what will you be doing
while I'm driving this?

03:50.062 --> 03:51.063
Me?

03:52.022 --> 03:53.274
That.

03:58.821 --> 04:00.239
- Start it.
- Okay.

04:00.865 --> 04:02.032
That's it.

04:02.116 --> 04:04.410
Step on the clutch and just push forward.

04:05.077 --> 04:08.289
That's it. Gently. That's it.
It's okay. You're okay.

04:08.372 --> 04:11.041
- Should I go?
- Yes. Step on it a bit.

04:11.125 --> 04:13.461
- This thing is so loud.
- No, look over here.

04:14.962 --> 04:16.547
- Isn't this too fast?
- Easy, right?

04:16.630 --> 04:18.758
- Yeah.
- Okay, turn left here.

04:18.841 --> 04:19.842
Left turn?

04:38.611 --> 04:39.612
That's it.

04:40.404 --> 04:41.655
That's it.

05:07.640 --> 05:08.974
Let me touch it.

05:14.313 --> 05:15.314
I'll take this one.

05:17.983 --> 05:19.568
- Which mask do you want?
- What?

05:20.110 --> 05:21.111
I don't want it.

05:25.157 --> 05:28.577
We have to lure them in.
We're going to lead them over here.

05:28.661 --> 05:29.662
Time it perfectly.

05:29.745 --> 05:31.872
Counting the guys from China,
there are going to be a lot of them.

05:31.956 --> 05:34.124
What's the most important thing? Timing.

05:37.044 --> 05:38.420
We're all set, right?

05:38.504 --> 05:42.216
- Yes. It's perfect.
- It's been so long since my last bust.

05:42.299 --> 05:44.301
My heart is pounding.

05:46.011 --> 05:49.223
Well, it looks like we're ready,
so let's get something to eat.

05:49.306 --> 05:52.268
- What?
- How can you eat before this?

05:52.393 --> 05:55.729
I'm suggesting it for your sake.
You're so weak that you got beaten up.

05:56.230 --> 05:57.606
I'll make you strong.

05:59.608 --> 06:01.527
- You got money?
- You should pay.

06:02.111 --> 06:03.320
You're the oldest.

06:04.029 --> 06:07.366
KOREAN BEEF

06:17.167 --> 06:18.210
That's delicious.

06:31.307 --> 06:32.725
Slow down a little.

06:33.392 --> 06:34.894
Doesn't your boss buy you meat?

06:35.019 --> 06:37.062
I'm so used to eating
expired store lunch boxes.

06:37.271 --> 06:38.606
I never get to have proper beef.

06:39.106 --> 06:40.107
This is amazing.

06:40.190 --> 06:42.776
Real Korean beef is on another level.

06:43.485 --> 06:44.528
He only fed you expired food?

06:45.362 --> 06:48.532
- What a scumbag boss.
- Who are you calling a scumbag boss?

06:48.616 --> 06:50.826
When did I only feed you
expired food, bastard?

06:50.910 --> 06:53.495
Every day.
And only the most unpopular ones.

06:53.579 --> 06:54.872
I fed you other stuff!

06:54.955 --> 06:57.124
I know it's a tough world out there.

06:57.207 --> 07:01.128
But how can you not buy this young man
some Korean beef?

07:01.211 --> 07:04.506
Have the bibimbap with the noodles.
It tastes better that way.

07:04.590 --> 07:06.383
- Really? Can I do that?
- Of course.

07:06.467 --> 07:08.218
I'm going to eat till I burst.

07:08.302 --> 07:11.555
You're gonna make people think
I never buy you anything.

07:11.639 --> 07:13.140
Hey, we were busy with the store.

07:13.223 --> 07:16.226
We didn't have time because
it was just the two of us running it.

07:17.061 --> 07:18.604
And besides...

07:18.687 --> 07:20.731
I haven't had much beef in my life either.

07:22.024 --> 07:24.485
But why did you work so hard
at the convenience store?

07:26.528 --> 07:29.198
Well, he worked hard,
so I just worked hard too.

07:29.281 --> 07:32.326
- Do you need a reason to work hard?
- You even got an award.

07:32.409 --> 07:34.536
For "Friendly Convenience Store"
or something.

07:35.996 --> 07:38.540
Maybe that's a better fit
than being a gangster, huh?

07:38.624 --> 07:39.959
No way.

07:40.042 --> 07:42.586
His calling is being number two
in the Hwasan Sect.

07:42.670 --> 07:45.381
He's just being patient now
to avenge the big boss.

07:45.464 --> 07:47.132
- Isn't that right?
- Something like that.

07:47.216 --> 07:51.261
I can't believe you got an award
for friendliness.

07:52.805 --> 07:55.975
Hey, what's wrong with being friendly?
It's not like it's impossible.

07:56.058 --> 07:59.728
This guy lived undercover for ten years.

08:00.437 --> 08:02.439
What are you talking about? Undercover?

08:02.523 --> 08:05.317
Come on, Mr. Jeong. Be honest with us.

08:06.068 --> 08:07.903
Did you marry your wife
because you loved her?

08:08.445 --> 08:12.616
I mean, we saw you get married,
and we saw you have a child.

08:12.700 --> 08:13.784
But we couldn't believe it.

08:13.867 --> 08:15.327
Because in movies, right?

08:15.411 --> 08:18.414
Agents get married and
do all sorts of things for their cover.

08:19.331 --> 08:20.416
Huh?

08:20.833 --> 08:22.668
Did you give him an order to get married?

08:23.419 --> 08:25.963
Why would I go as far as
ordering him to marry?

08:26.046 --> 08:28.799
- You watch too many movies.
- No, that's not it.

08:28.882 --> 08:31.969
There's a limit
to how much a man can be whipped.

08:32.511 --> 08:34.972
It's almost impossible to believe
how low he ranks in his family.

08:35.639 --> 08:37.474
- For real?
- So that's the real you?

08:37.599 --> 08:40.102
Hey, what do you people take me for?

08:40.185 --> 08:42.312
You got married as a cover
to work at the restaurant, right?

08:43.647 --> 08:44.982
Hey, stop eating!

08:46.817 --> 08:48.277
I'm not buying you food
to take all this crap.

08:48.360 --> 08:49.528
- Stop eating!
- Come on!

08:49.611 --> 08:51.405
- What's with you?
- You only get to eat the sauce!

08:51.488 --> 08:54.074
This is just bad table manners!
We get it already!

08:54.908 --> 08:57.745
It's not even that expensive.
I checked the price on my way in.

08:57.828 --> 09:00.205
Hey, it won't be that much.
Order whatever you want.

09:00.289 --> 09:02.499
Plus, you're not even buying.
He's taking care of it.

09:02.583 --> 09:03.625
- Really?
- Order more!

09:03.709 --> 09:05.544
Ma'am, can we get some more meat?

09:07.129 --> 09:09.506
Wow, look at the quality of this.

09:14.595 --> 09:15.888
What are you doing?

09:23.353 --> 09:24.646
I've got a lot on my mind.

09:26.940 --> 09:30.194
Like you said, I've lived as
a convenience store owner for ten years.

09:31.153 --> 09:33.822
I'm worried if I can pull this off.

09:36.200 --> 09:37.326
Getting scared again?

09:38.535 --> 09:40.746
Why do you keep saying I'm scared?

09:40.829 --> 09:42.831
You think I'd be scared
of that bastard Yoo In-gu?

09:43.540 --> 09:46.293
It's just that they've got a lot of men.

09:46.752 --> 09:50.005
And I got my ass beaten
because I overestimated myself.

09:51.423 --> 09:53.842
So naturally, I've been having doubts.

09:54.843 --> 09:56.345
Maybe my body can't take this.

09:58.764 --> 09:59.932
What about you?

10:00.766 --> 10:02.267
Aren't you worried?

10:02.810 --> 10:04.019
Is your body

10:04.937 --> 10:06.146
like it was ten years ago?

10:08.524 --> 10:12.986
If I was the same as ten years ago,
do you think I'd have worked with you?

10:15.572 --> 10:19.034
There's nothing to be scared of.
My calculations are never off.

10:19.118 --> 10:21.120
You, Ma Gong-bok, Seong-won, and me?

10:21.787 --> 10:25.124
We may be washed up,
but we'd never lose to Yoo In-gu.

10:25.249 --> 10:27.417
So don't you worry.

10:28.460 --> 10:30.170
Just stick to the plan.

10:31.588 --> 10:33.465
Then you won't get your ass kicked alone.

10:34.716 --> 10:35.759
Well, well.

10:36.510 --> 10:38.137
Now it feels like a real alliance.

10:39.221 --> 10:40.639
Fine, we've come this far.

10:41.807 --> 10:43.142
I'll trust you this once.

10:44.852 --> 10:45.853
Damn it.

11:05.539 --> 11:06.874
You guys go on ahead.

11:08.834 --> 11:10.127
What? You're not coming?

11:10.919 --> 11:12.713
You said we were doing a final check.

11:12.796 --> 11:15.007
No, there's somewhere I need to be.

11:15.132 --> 11:16.884
Where are you going all of a sudden?

11:18.844 --> 11:19.845
Something came up.

11:19.928 --> 11:23.140
The big bust is just around the corner,
and something came up?

11:23.223 --> 11:24.683
You think I have nothing to do?

11:24.766 --> 11:26.894
I've got a million things
to check before closing.

11:26.977 --> 11:29.855
We have a lot to go over.
Where are you going?

11:34.818 --> 11:35.819
It's all right.

11:36.195 --> 11:37.571
Don't worry about it. Just go.

11:38.155 --> 11:39.907
Go on. I'll take care of things here.

11:40.032 --> 11:41.491
Huh? What's gotten into you?

11:45.037 --> 11:48.332
- But what about the operation?
- I'll handle it. Let's go.

11:48.415 --> 11:50.751
How can we do that without him?

11:50.834 --> 11:52.878
We've gone over it enough. We'll be fine.

11:52.961 --> 11:54.630
Yeah, but he's the one who planned it.

12:03.972 --> 12:06.725
You know where he went, don't you?

12:07.351 --> 12:10.145
He just went to take care of something.

12:10.229 --> 12:12.314
He just remembered he had an errand to run

12:12.397 --> 12:13.857
just hours before the operation?

12:14.399 --> 12:16.193
Be honest. Did something happen?

12:17.194 --> 12:18.862
It's not that.

12:18.946 --> 12:21.365
Gong-bok brought up family earlier.

12:21.490 --> 12:23.575
- I think it got to him.
- Family?

12:23.659 --> 12:25.202
What did I say about family?

12:25.827 --> 12:28.330
Oh, you mean
when I joked about his marriage?

12:29.373 --> 12:31.750
- So his marriage really is a sham?
- Don't ever say that!

12:32.709 --> 12:34.211
That's not it.

12:34.294 --> 12:36.672
It's Ho-myeong's first operation
since he's had a family.

12:36.755 --> 12:38.757
So he probably has a lot on his mind.

12:38.840 --> 12:41.677
He knows better than anyone
just how evil Han Gyeong-wook is.

12:43.053 --> 12:46.139
You mean he knows him?
Jeong Ho-myeong and Han Gyeong-wook?

12:46.974 --> 12:48.892
Did they know each other
before the ferry case?

12:54.523 --> 12:57.567
- I shouldn't have said anything.
- No, you have to tell us.

12:57.651 --> 13:00.821
The guy's pulling a stunt like this
right before the operation.

13:00.946 --> 13:02.864
We have a right to know why, don't we?

13:05.617 --> 13:07.619
When Ho-myeong was with the NIS

13:08.370 --> 13:11.081
he used to work on the same team
as Han Gyeong-wook.

13:11.164 --> 13:14.167
- They were on the same team?
- Yeah.

13:16.420 --> 13:19.381
For a long time, until that incident.

13:19.464 --> 13:20.882
They were partners.

13:21.591 --> 13:24.761
12 YEARS AGO

13:43.780 --> 13:44.823
I'm in.

13:46.074 --> 13:47.492
You sure the mole is here?

13:47.576 --> 13:50.203
Positive.
That mole has leaked crucial intel.

13:50.287 --> 13:52.247
It's gotten a lot of our agents killed.

13:52.331 --> 13:55.792
We can't let a traitor like that run away
without paying for what he's done.

13:55.876 --> 13:58.086
You're to shoot to kill on sight.

13:58.170 --> 13:59.546
Roger that.

14:36.458 --> 14:38.126
You know why I'm here, don't you?

14:56.103 --> 14:57.771
- You...
- Ho-myeong.

14:58.647 --> 15:01.316
- Just listen to me.
- It was you?

15:02.359 --> 15:05.487
- The traitor who sold out his own people?
- No. You know me.

15:06.029 --> 15:10.534
You know how hard I worked
for the sake of our nation.

15:10.867 --> 15:13.078
Then why are you not in North Korea?

15:13.912 --> 15:16.665
Deputy Director Han confirmed it himself.

15:17.499 --> 15:20.961
That the traitor would be here today
to sell the intel on our agents.

15:21.711 --> 15:23.046
Ho-myeong.

15:24.381 --> 15:25.841
You're being played by him.

15:27.300 --> 15:28.385
He framed me.

15:29.177 --> 15:30.720
He forced me to live on the run.

15:31.972 --> 15:33.974
- It was Deputy Director Han.
- Shut up.

15:34.933 --> 15:35.934
Why would he do that?

15:36.017 --> 15:38.937
Han is up to something.

15:40.439 --> 15:42.065
He thought I'd figure it out.

15:44.818 --> 15:46.069
So he's trying to get rid of me.

15:47.404 --> 15:49.156
What exactly is he up to?

15:49.698 --> 15:51.992
- Can you prove it?
- Well...

15:57.914 --> 15:58.915
Ho-myeong.

15:59.791 --> 16:00.792
Ten minutes.

16:01.793 --> 16:03.670
- What?
- Just give me ten minutes.

16:06.131 --> 16:07.132
My daughter will be here.

16:08.008 --> 16:10.302
I only saw her as a baby six years ago.

16:11.386 --> 16:12.429
Please.

16:13.430 --> 16:15.015
Let me have one dinner with her.

16:18.602 --> 16:20.979
- You're lying.
- I'm not lying.

16:21.897 --> 16:23.064
Just ten minutes.

16:24.232 --> 16:26.151
She'll be here in ten minutes.

16:26.234 --> 16:29.654
We'll just have dinner together,
and I'll go with you.

16:31.239 --> 16:33.408
After that, you can do
whatever you want with me.

16:34.284 --> 16:35.285
Ho-myeong.

16:36.036 --> 16:37.329
I'll come with you

16:37.412 --> 16:38.455
and tell you all about Han's--

16:45.921 --> 16:47.172
Sir.

17:09.110 --> 17:11.988
I believe my orders
were to eliminate him on sight.

17:13.698 --> 17:16.701
I came by just in case. Good thing I did.

17:18.745 --> 17:21.206
Jeong Ho-myeong, you're an agent.

17:21.831 --> 17:23.500
Did you seriously believe his crap?

17:23.583 --> 17:25.794
He used to be part of your team, sir.

17:26.545 --> 17:29.881
Shouldn't we have at least heard him out?

17:31.049 --> 17:32.551
Heard him out?

17:34.344 --> 17:35.512
It's just...

17:36.179 --> 17:39.516
He said he wasn't here to make a deal.
He said his daughter was coming.

17:40.767 --> 17:42.435
He said he'd come with us after they eat.

17:45.146 --> 17:46.773
And you believe that crap?

17:48.316 --> 17:49.818
Where is his daughter then?

17:54.197 --> 17:58.660
You know that such sentiments
are just a weakness for an agent.

18:03.206 --> 18:04.958
I've wasted enough time on this.

18:07.460 --> 18:08.795
Clean up this mess.

19:08.563 --> 19:10.649
That incident must've been
a huge shock to him.

19:10.732 --> 19:13.652
He asked to be taken off field duty
several times.

19:14.653 --> 19:15.987
But it was denied every time.

19:18.198 --> 19:21.451
If Han Gyeong-wook found out
that Ho-myeong is married and has a son...

19:22.285 --> 19:23.620
There's no telling what he'd do.

19:24.412 --> 19:27.749
Ho-myeong never showed it,
but he must have been worried.

19:39.636 --> 19:42.055
You want me to pull out
from the restaurant?

19:42.138 --> 19:43.139
7 YEARS AGO

19:43.223 --> 19:44.766
Yeah.

19:44.849 --> 19:47.811
You've been here all this time
without a single sign of Bulgae.

19:47.936 --> 19:49.729
I know, but still.

19:51.356 --> 19:53.108
Is it really necessary to move?

19:53.191 --> 19:56.027
Staying in one place too long
could compromise your cover.

19:56.111 --> 19:57.445
You know that.

19:59.072 --> 20:01.866
It's time to move.
Start wrapping things up.

20:04.744 --> 20:06.246
Yeah. Okay.

20:08.832 --> 20:10.125
Wrap things up.

20:13.670 --> 20:14.671
There.

20:15.088 --> 20:17.549
- Here's your jjamppong.
- Thank you.

20:47.328 --> 20:49.497
- Hey, Ho-myeong.
- Yeah?

20:50.081 --> 20:53.877
I have to talk to you about something
after we close.

20:54.544 --> 20:56.296
- To me?
- Yeah.

21:02.552 --> 21:04.721
No, I'm not drinking.

21:05.680 --> 21:08.641
- Why not?
- Well, the thing is...

21:14.773 --> 21:15.815
Ho-myeong.

21:16.733 --> 21:19.068
Remember how I said
I haven't been feeling well lately?

21:19.694 --> 21:21.154
You're still not feeling well?

21:23.239 --> 21:24.657
Well...

21:24.741 --> 21:26.242
I'm pregnant.

21:37.045 --> 21:38.463
Pregnant?

21:40.089 --> 21:43.843
I went to the doctor yesterday.
I'm eight weeks in.

21:48.264 --> 21:50.683
I'm not telling you this to pressure you.

21:51.059 --> 21:52.936
I'll handle it.

21:53.061 --> 21:54.562
What do you mean you'll handle it?

21:57.065 --> 21:59.526
Honestly, you and I?

22:00.401 --> 22:04.572
What we have is just a fling, isn't it?

22:06.950 --> 22:08.326
What are you saying?

22:10.703 --> 22:15.625
We've been seeing each other
for a long time.

22:16.668 --> 22:18.169
But I don't know much about you.

22:19.420 --> 22:20.880
Barely anything, really.

22:21.881 --> 22:26.469
Like who you were before,
or why you came to Yeongseon Island.

22:27.387 --> 22:31.558
I've never even heard you mention
your parents, siblings, or friends.

22:33.059 --> 22:34.185
And you don't...

22:34.936 --> 22:36.980
You don't exactly have plans

22:37.730 --> 22:39.232
to tell me

22:40.275 --> 22:42.485
about any of that, do you?

22:52.078 --> 22:55.832
I'm almost 40,
so having a baby is a bit...

22:56.749 --> 22:57.750
scary.

22:58.710 --> 23:01.546
And even if I had a baby,

23:01.629 --> 23:03.381
I'd have no idea how to raise it.

23:03.464 --> 23:05.133
Plus, I'm busy with the store.

23:06.134 --> 23:08.970
I've said what I needed to say,
so just enjoy your drink.

23:09.971 --> 23:11.222
I'm not drinking.

23:12.015 --> 23:13.016
Huh?

23:16.811 --> 23:18.187
I won't drink alone.

23:19.731 --> 23:21.065
Let's drink after the baby is born.

23:25.028 --> 23:26.029
What...

23:26.863 --> 23:29.157
What do you mean by that?

23:31.075 --> 23:32.201
Let's have this baby.

23:33.411 --> 23:36.873
Is it really that simple for you?

23:36.956 --> 23:38.291
It's not.

23:40.460 --> 23:41.753
The truth is...

23:43.504 --> 23:45.256
My parents passed away when I was young.

23:47.008 --> 23:48.635
So I never had a family.

23:50.261 --> 23:52.931
I never thought about things
like marriage or kids.

23:54.432 --> 23:56.726
I've never even thought
about starting my own family.

23:58.311 --> 24:00.730
But when you just told me
you were pregnant...

24:01.481 --> 24:02.482
I mean...

24:03.274 --> 24:05.360
I don't know what this feeling is.

24:06.945 --> 24:08.029
But it made me think...

24:10.615 --> 24:13.201
That no matter what happens

24:14.661 --> 24:16.245
I want to be with you and our child.

24:19.332 --> 24:21.709
Let's get married, O-ran.

24:46.025 --> 24:47.986
Ho-myeong, why are you out here?

24:48.069 --> 24:50.947
- Why aren't you coming in?
- Oh, you scared me.

24:51.030 --> 24:53.157
Didn't you come here
to make up with O-ran?

24:59.038 --> 25:00.873
You brought the letter, right?

25:01.958 --> 25:04.043
- No.
- What? Why not?

25:04.127 --> 25:05.253
Well, I just...

25:06.254 --> 25:10.717
- I didn't know what to write.
- You still don't get O-ran?

25:10.800 --> 25:15.013
She'll forgive you
if you just say the right things.

25:15.096 --> 25:17.265
She's that easygoing, just like me.

25:18.891 --> 25:22.478
Well, this time,
I don't know if a few words will do.

25:23.855 --> 25:25.565
And I'm the one at fault.

25:25.690 --> 25:28.443
I think I'll just make her angrier.

25:33.322 --> 25:36.868
Do you know
why I came to Yeongseon Island?

25:38.536 --> 25:39.746
You said it was your hometown.

25:39.829 --> 25:41.247
It's not.

25:41.330 --> 25:43.458
I was going to open a store in Seoul.

25:43.541 --> 25:46.169
But I lost the money in a scam,
so I had no choice.

25:46.711 --> 25:47.712
What?

25:48.713 --> 25:52.508
I couldn't tell my wife.
My pride wouldn't let me.

25:53.176 --> 25:55.178
So I just lied to her.

25:55.261 --> 25:58.431
I told her wanted to settle down
in my hometown.

26:00.308 --> 26:03.895
My wife must have suspected something.

26:03.978 --> 26:05.605
But she didn't say a word.

26:05.688 --> 26:08.483
Even though she was pregnant,
she followed me without a complaint.

26:09.567 --> 26:12.320
I figured if she knew I'd been scammed,
she'd only be heartbroken.

26:12.403 --> 26:13.863
So I kept it from her.

26:13.946 --> 26:18.326
I thought I'd tell her
once the restaurant had found its place.

26:18.409 --> 26:19.702
But then...

26:20.828 --> 26:22.455
I never got to tell her.

26:26.793 --> 26:29.337
I should have just told her.

26:30.463 --> 26:32.673
Why did she work so hard every day?

26:32.757 --> 26:34.050
She wasn't well.

26:35.176 --> 26:37.637
She never even made time
to go to a hospital.

26:42.100 --> 26:43.226
I wish I'd told her.

26:44.227 --> 26:46.896
Maybe she would've hated me
a little less when she passed.

26:52.151 --> 26:54.278
Don't leave any stupid regrets like I did.

26:54.362 --> 26:56.114
Be open with each other.

26:56.197 --> 26:59.242
That's what marriage is all about, right?

26:59.992 --> 27:01.244
Don't let O-ran...

27:02.161 --> 27:03.996
Don't let my daughter
be upset for so long.

27:07.291 --> 27:11.129
- Yes, I understand.
- Yeah? Let's go right now.

27:11.212 --> 27:13.840
Right now, I have something
I need to sort out.

27:14.674 --> 27:17.969
Next time I'm around, I'll tell her.

27:18.052 --> 27:23.891
I'll tell O-ran everything
that I haven't been able to.

27:25.685 --> 27:26.936
Geez.

27:28.646 --> 27:29.730
You know, right?

27:30.439 --> 27:31.941
An apology is all about timing.

27:33.401 --> 27:35.987
Yes. I won't be too late.

27:47.874 --> 27:51.836
It's been forever
since I've had the spotlight.

27:51.919 --> 27:53.129
I'm getting nervous.

27:54.964 --> 27:56.924
Give me one last update, will you?

27:57.675 --> 27:59.635
You've cut off
all funding for the orphanage, right?

28:01.053 --> 28:03.014
Oh, you shouldn't have.

28:10.521 --> 28:14.150
Thanks to Deputy Director Han,
it all went smoothly.

28:14.734 --> 28:15.735
Sir!

28:15.818 --> 28:19.030
We could say they didn't qualify
due to their outdated facilities.

28:19.113 --> 28:21.949
It's not even
the scheduled inspection date.

28:22.033 --> 28:24.577
It's a surprise inspection, ma'am.

28:24.660 --> 28:26.954
If we gave you a notice,
how would it be a surprise?

28:28.414 --> 28:30.416
Their financial situation is obvious.

28:30.499 --> 28:32.460
It's true that
the facilities are outdated.

28:32.543 --> 28:36.756
But still, if you do this so suddenly,
where are our children supposed to go?

28:36.839 --> 28:39.967
In any case, we have issued a warning
as per protocol.

28:40.051 --> 28:42.303
You can either use your own money
to make the repairs

28:42.386 --> 28:43.679
or shut the place down.

28:43.763 --> 28:45.181
Whatever you need to do.

28:45.264 --> 28:49.894
With no money to fix up the place,
they'll end up doing as we intended.

28:49.977 --> 28:52.855
- What about donors?
- They didn't have any major ones.

28:52.939 --> 28:56.651
Besides government subsidies,
it's all small donations from individuals.

28:56.734 --> 29:00.321
And most of that is Kim Seon-jung
and his wife's personal funds.

29:01.030 --> 29:04.033
That's why it's a problem
when you're too squeaky clean.

29:04.867 --> 29:06.452
Okay, good job.

29:06.535 --> 29:08.079
Now then.

29:08.829 --> 29:12.541
Shall I go and help myself
to the feast that's been laid out?

29:17.004 --> 29:18.756
Hello, sir.

29:18.839 --> 29:21.676
- How have you been?
- Good. How about you?

29:21.759 --> 29:22.802
That's good.

29:22.885 --> 29:24.345
Why can't we take out a loan?

29:24.428 --> 29:25.471
I'm sorry.

29:25.554 --> 29:27.723
But our decision is based on an evaluation

29:27.807 --> 29:29.767
of your credit rating
and collateral value.

29:29.850 --> 29:33.437
Your loan application
was denied in our internal review.

29:33.521 --> 29:36.065
But the manager said it was possible.

29:36.148 --> 29:38.734
Could you please check one more time?

29:43.072 --> 29:45.283
Excuse me, sir.

29:48.244 --> 29:51.247
- Oh, ma'am, what brings you here?
- Hello, sir.

29:51.330 --> 29:55.167
Ma'am, please, let's not do this here.
You can talk to me.

29:55.251 --> 29:56.419
Please.

29:56.502 --> 30:00.965
Why was the loan suddenly denied?
We're going to have to shut down.

30:01.048 --> 30:03.634
What are we supposed to do
with the children?

30:03.718 --> 30:05.219
Ah, excuse me.

30:06.053 --> 30:09.932
- What children?
- Oh, this lady runs an orphanage.

30:10.016 --> 30:12.101
And it seems there's been
a misunderstanding.

30:13.269 --> 30:17.231
Well, if you don't mind,
may I listen in on what she has to say?

30:17.690 --> 30:20.985
It's just that I don't quite understand
what's going on.

30:21.068 --> 30:25.823
This lady seems like a wonderful person
who dedicates herself to society.

30:26.407 --> 30:28.617
What's the reason
her loan was suddenly denied?

30:29.368 --> 30:31.287
Well, the thing is...

30:31.829 --> 30:35.624
When it comes to loans,
there are various policy-related factors.

30:36.500 --> 30:38.627
Exactly, those policies.

30:38.711 --> 30:42.214
They don't just change overnight, do they?
What do you think?

30:42.298 --> 30:45.426
Exactly.
You said it wasn't a problem last time.

30:45.509 --> 30:48.721
Sir, are you sure
you've reviewed this properly?

30:48.804 --> 30:49.930
Uh, well, that's...

30:50.014 --> 30:53.517
I've never seen a bank
change a loan policy overnight.

30:53.934 --> 30:55.895
I'm rapidly losing my faith
in this establishment.

30:56.604 --> 30:59.607
Who knows?
I could be in that lady's shoes.

31:00.274 --> 31:02.777
And you might
just flip on me just as easily.

31:02.860 --> 31:04.153
No, I would...

31:05.029 --> 31:06.614
That's... Ms. Kim.

31:07.198 --> 31:09.575
Bring me the documents
for the lady's loan.

31:09.658 --> 31:12.119
- I'll take a look myself.
- Yes, sir. Right away.

31:12.203 --> 31:13.245
Quickly.

31:15.873 --> 31:17.083
Excuse me.

31:18.751 --> 31:21.087
I never got a chance to thank you.

31:21.170 --> 31:22.671
Thank you so much.

31:22.755 --> 31:25.424
Oh, it was nothing.
Was everything resolved?

31:25.549 --> 31:26.926
Yes.

31:27.009 --> 31:29.053
Thanks to you,
I think the loan will be approved.

31:30.137 --> 31:33.808
- I can't thank you enough.
- Oh, never mind, never mind.

31:34.266 --> 31:37.978
You were so worried
the children would wind up on the streets.

31:39.397 --> 31:41.023
It reminded me of my past.

31:42.650 --> 31:45.277
When I was young,
my father's business failed.

31:45.403 --> 31:47.238
And I was homeless in the Philippines.

31:47.321 --> 31:49.073
Oh, no. Really?

31:49.156 --> 31:52.368
I made a promise to myself back then.

31:53.411 --> 31:57.081
That I would never turn my back
on someone in need.

31:57.373 --> 32:00.376
But I'd forgotten all about it
just because I got a little busy.

32:00.459 --> 32:04.588
You clearly haven't.
You helped our children so much today.

32:04.713 --> 32:06.632
Not at all. On the contrary.

32:07.466 --> 32:11.512
Meeting you today has made me
reflect on a lot of things.

32:11.595 --> 32:14.056
I've been so focused on getting ahead

32:14.140 --> 32:17.601
that I haven't looked
at the world around me.

32:17.685 --> 32:19.478
And frankly, I'm ashamed of myself.

32:21.772 --> 32:23.232
Which brings me to my point.

32:23.315 --> 32:25.317
You don't have to say yes.

32:25.401 --> 32:29.363
But would it be okay
if I sent a small gift to the children?

32:29.447 --> 32:32.116
- What?
- Ah, a gift. Yes?

32:33.242 --> 32:35.661
As long as you follow
the proper procedure.

32:35.744 --> 32:39.582
Oh, it's not that big of a gift
that'd require formal procedures.

32:40.166 --> 32:42.877
As long as you say yes, that is.

32:44.879 --> 32:47.923
We try to run our organization
as transparently as possible.

32:48.048 --> 32:52.136
We don't accept any private donations
of cash or goods.

32:52.219 --> 32:54.930
I'm sorry, but we'll only have to
accept your kind words.

32:55.014 --> 32:56.265
No.

32:56.348 --> 33:00.436
It's really not a big deal at all,
so I'm actually a bit embarrassed.

33:01.729 --> 33:05.357
Have we disposed of all the old books
from our hotel lounge?

33:05.441 --> 33:07.568
- Not yet.
- All right.

33:08.277 --> 33:11.530
It may not be much,
but what if I gave them these books?

33:11.614 --> 33:14.033
The idea just popped into my head.

33:14.158 --> 33:17.578
- Oh, the books?
- Yes. The books.

33:17.661 --> 33:20.998
It's not money or material things.
Just food for thought?

33:22.124 --> 33:26.462
It's just a few old books.
Would that be a problem too?

33:30.049 --> 33:32.176
WE OPPOSE YEONGSEON REDEVELOPMENT

33:57.743 --> 34:00.955
It was brief,
but the way he moved was not ordinary.

34:04.750 --> 34:06.418
And he has amnesia?

34:07.294 --> 34:09.880
There's so much
that's suspicious about him.

34:15.719 --> 34:20.224
Look. Prosecutor Gang has been
staring at Je-sun like that for a while.

34:20.307 --> 34:23.811
Something's definitely
going on between them.

34:24.728 --> 34:27.648
No way.
She just looks like she wants a fight.

34:27.731 --> 34:28.941
What would you know?

34:29.441 --> 34:30.484
You've never had a man.

34:38.993 --> 34:41.829
Mr. Bong.
Something happened between you two, right?

34:44.373 --> 34:46.041
Nothing happened.

34:46.125 --> 34:48.711
I was quite the heartbreaker
back in my day.

34:49.378 --> 34:51.714
When a woman gives you a look like that?

34:51.839 --> 34:55.175
It's either you owe her money,
or she's into you.

34:58.804 --> 35:00.514
It's so delicious.

35:03.601 --> 35:04.768
Be honest.

35:04.852 --> 35:06.687
You're into her too, aren't you?

35:06.770 --> 35:09.982
Come on, it's not like that. It's just...

35:11.066 --> 35:13.402
I mean, we've gotten kind of close.

35:13.944 --> 35:17.948
I'm just gonna bring the Sergeant
some soup in.

35:25.164 --> 35:26.749
Busy, busy.

35:28.334 --> 35:29.668
This was so delicious.

35:30.669 --> 35:32.046
I'll do the dishes tomorrow.

35:44.642 --> 35:46.143
Eat up.

35:49.647 --> 35:52.316
Hey, mister. Could you untie me, please?

35:52.399 --> 35:54.568
I'm not a criminal. What is this?

35:54.652 --> 35:56.028
Eat up.

35:58.614 --> 36:00.741
Come on, how can I eat
with my hands tied like this?

36:07.623 --> 36:08.999
Eat up.

36:11.835 --> 36:13.587
Damn it.

36:13.671 --> 36:15.589
This is a felony, you know that?

36:15.673 --> 36:20.344
The real felony is what you
and the Heaven Capital guys committed.

36:20.928 --> 36:24.014
Fine, don't eat if you don't want to.
What a waste of rice. Jeez.

36:24.723 --> 36:26.058
Wait, wait.

36:26.809 --> 36:30.270
Wait, are you the martial arts master
Heaven Capital was looking for?

36:30.396 --> 36:32.106
You fought them 17 to 1? Or was it 18?

36:32.189 --> 36:34.108
And the way you moved yesterday...

36:34.191 --> 36:35.484
It is you!

36:35.567 --> 36:36.694
Listen, sir.

36:36.777 --> 36:38.070
It's a pleasure to meet you.

36:38.153 --> 36:39.321
Please untie me.

36:39.405 --> 36:41.824
If you let me go,
I'll have a word with those guys.

36:41.907 --> 36:44.702
I'll tell them to stop chasing you.

36:44.785 --> 36:45.828
I promise. Okay?

36:50.165 --> 36:51.792
Just, uh... Eat your food.

37:11.353 --> 37:12.855
What the...

37:13.939 --> 37:15.149
What are you doing?

37:17.609 --> 37:20.362
Oh, I felt so dizzy
that I had to lean against the door.

37:25.367 --> 37:26.368
Goodness.

37:38.672 --> 37:39.673
Go ahead and eat.

37:45.512 --> 37:50.184
Here we go.

37:55.606 --> 37:56.857
You look cheerful.

37:57.316 --> 37:59.610
Feeling better
now that the loan came through?

38:00.611 --> 38:03.280
Of course. I was worried sick.

38:03.614 --> 38:08.202
Guess what? Someone I met at the bank
wants to make a donation.

38:09.495 --> 38:11.246
A donation? Who?

38:11.330 --> 38:15.375
Chairman Do Hyeon-tae of the Heaven Hotel.
He said they have used books.

38:15.501 --> 38:17.920
He'd rather donate them to the kids
than throw them away.

38:20.172 --> 38:21.215
Do Hyeon-tae...

38:22.549 --> 38:23.884
The Chairman of Heaven Casino?

38:25.761 --> 38:28.764
He's never shown any interest
in public service.

38:29.181 --> 38:30.974
Why suddenly make a donation?

38:33.644 --> 38:34.812
That's odd.

38:37.731 --> 38:40.150
Honey, you have to turn it down.

38:41.652 --> 38:42.653
What?

38:43.403 --> 38:46.198
It's a book donation, not money.

38:46.281 --> 38:50.410
Still, who knows
what the man is really after?

38:50.494 --> 38:53.205
Anyway, don't take anything from him,
books or otherwise.

38:53.288 --> 38:55.499
You've really turned into a politician,
haven't you?

38:55.582 --> 38:57.626
It was a kind offer.

38:57.709 --> 38:59.753
And you can't see it
as anything but suspicious?

38:59.837 --> 39:02.172
That's not it.
I'm just saying we should be careful.

39:02.256 --> 39:05.384
It's just a few used books.
What is there to be so careful about?

39:05.467 --> 39:08.345
Should the children go without books
because of your political ambitions?

39:17.312 --> 39:20.065
You're right. I overreacted.

39:20.148 --> 39:23.235
It's just a few used books.
Take them. All right?

39:23.819 --> 39:25.821
- Really?
- Yeah.

39:34.329 --> 39:38.625
Chairman, we've received the used books.

39:38.709 --> 39:41.003
Thank you for your generous donation.

39:42.129 --> 39:43.755
Your kindness

39:43.839 --> 39:47.217
will be food for the soul
for everyone here.

39:52.180 --> 39:54.141
The package is delivered.

39:56.685 --> 39:59.730
I made a special selection
from my most prized collections.

40:00.981 --> 40:03.191
You didn't just drop them off
and leave, did you?

40:04.318 --> 40:05.819
Of course not.

40:05.903 --> 40:08.864
I've already spoken to an employee.

40:10.407 --> 40:12.784
I told him he'd be ruined
by gambling debts

40:12.868 --> 40:15.537
if he didn't get rid of
those paintings for us.

40:16.371 --> 40:19.333
It's to be sold off without her knowing,
and the money will be discreetly deposited

40:19.416 --> 40:22.377
into the organization's bank account
as a donation.

40:22.461 --> 40:24.838
Just push the button

40:24.922 --> 40:27.758
and Kim Seon-jung will no longer be

40:27.841 --> 40:29.885
the honest mayoral candidate
everyone loves.

40:29.968 --> 40:33.388
He'll be a man who used a charity
to raise illegal political funds.

40:33.847 --> 40:36.308
A corrupt politician
who's no better than trash.

40:39.770 --> 40:41.813
- Well done.
- Thank you.

40:42.397 --> 40:43.440
So...

40:43.941 --> 40:45.067
Shall I set off the package?

40:45.192 --> 40:46.568
If we're going to set it off

40:47.527 --> 40:49.446
it might as well be a good show.

40:49.988 --> 40:51.865
- What do you mean?
- Baek.

40:52.240 --> 40:53.241
Yes.

40:53.742 --> 40:56.912
Let's go grab some soup soon.

40:57.037 --> 40:58.205
Understood.

41:04.544 --> 41:06.046
Hey, what are you talking about?

41:06.129 --> 41:07.506
I was planning on going.

41:08.006 --> 41:10.676
But we've been after this broker
for the last three months.

41:10.968 --> 41:13.178
Hey, this is a huge case.

41:14.680 --> 41:16.098
Okay, just listen.

41:16.848 --> 41:19.059
If you can't make it,
at least send someone else.

41:19.142 --> 41:21.144
This broker is a big deal too.

41:21.436 --> 41:23.146
Plus, it's the chief's orders.

41:23.230 --> 41:24.773
Everyone here is on it.

41:24.856 --> 41:26.066
I'll be right behind you.

41:26.149 --> 41:27.150
Anyway...

41:27.234 --> 41:29.027
Please just gather some evidence for now.

41:29.111 --> 41:30.654
I'll be there as soon as I'm done.

41:30.737 --> 41:33.699
Screw the evidence.
You should be raiding the place!

41:33.782 --> 41:34.783
Hello?

41:39.955 --> 41:43.291
I thought they were just stealing money,
but they're bringing in drugs too.

41:44.334 --> 41:47.379
- You're the worst kind of scum.
- Look.

41:47.462 --> 41:50.382
These corrupt cops
and the Heaven Capital guys...

41:50.465 --> 41:54.970
If Prosecutor Gang links them to drugs,
can we really round them all up?

41:55.554 --> 41:57.472
We should be able to, right?

41:57.556 --> 41:59.599
It'll clean up the precinct, for sure.

41:59.683 --> 42:04.312
If they all go to prison,
everything they did will be revealed.

42:04.396 --> 42:06.648
If things go well,
I might get my house back.

42:07.733 --> 42:08.734
Hey, I'm sorry.

42:09.651 --> 42:12.487
I don't think the raid we planned
with the detectives today

42:12.571 --> 42:13.572
is going to happen.

42:13.655 --> 42:15.782
- Why not?
- What?

42:15.866 --> 42:18.285
So, are we supposed to
just sit here and watch?

42:18.368 --> 42:20.245
Oh, no. I'll go alone if I have to.

42:20.495 --> 42:23.081
I have to secure evidence
for there to be a next step.

42:23.373 --> 42:25.667
- All by yourself?
- Want to come with me then?

42:26.460 --> 42:28.920
Mi-kyung, would you mind coming with me?

42:29.004 --> 42:30.255
- Okay.
- Wait!

42:30.881 --> 42:32.758
I have to go too. I'm no civilian.

42:33.008 --> 42:35.302
- I'll be useful.
- I'm coming, too.

42:35.385 --> 42:37.721
I have to catch them to get my house back.

42:37.804 --> 42:39.723
I'll do anything. Please let me.

42:39.806 --> 42:43.810
Hold on.
That place is extremely dangerous.

42:44.352 --> 42:46.521
Then that's all the more reason
for us to go.

42:46.605 --> 42:48.732
We can't send you off all alone.

42:50.609 --> 42:51.610
- Right?
- Yes.

42:57.199 --> 42:58.742
- Welcome back, Boss!
- Welcome back, Boss!

42:59.367 --> 43:00.494
Is this everyone?

43:00.577 --> 43:01.578
Yes, Boss.

43:03.622 --> 43:07.459
As I told you before,
we must move without Han and Do noticing.

43:08.251 --> 43:09.252
This is the best we can do.

43:09.669 --> 43:12.506
Han and Do.
Those two are always getting in the way.

43:13.215 --> 43:14.424
Don't worry, sir.

43:14.508 --> 43:17.344
I have about thirty kids
on standby at the port.

43:17.761 --> 43:21.515
Martial arts master or not,
he can't handle that many people alone.

43:22.182 --> 43:24.017
Gotta make do with what we've got.

43:24.768 --> 43:27.270
Today is a historic day for the Ingu Sect.

43:28.105 --> 43:30.148
Anyone who screws up will die at my hand.

43:31.316 --> 43:34.111
- So you'd better stay sharp!
- Yes, Boss!

43:41.118 --> 43:43.120
- Hey, you're here.
- Hey, Jin-su.

43:43.245 --> 43:45.539
- Nam-il's here too.
- Heard the pay was good.

43:49.751 --> 43:53.463
- Why did you bring Nam-il?
- He said he was desperate for cash.

43:54.131 --> 43:55.132
Just cut him some slack.

43:56.091 --> 43:58.677
Hey, but what are we even doing here?

44:00.220 --> 44:02.180
- Why do we need these tools?
- Beats me.

44:37.841 --> 44:38.967
Evening, Boss!

44:39.676 --> 44:41.178
This kid's got some fight in him.

44:41.261 --> 44:43.305
- Get your head up.
- Yes, Boss!

44:43.763 --> 44:45.932
- Is everyone here?
- Yes! They're all here.

44:46.016 --> 44:47.642
- Okay. To your posts.
- To your posts!

44:52.189 --> 44:53.440
Listen up.

44:53.523 --> 44:57.235
A very important package
is arriving today for the Ingu Sect.

44:57.360 --> 45:01.781
Your job is to secure said package.

45:01.865 --> 45:03.700
And to make sure no one steals it.

45:04.993 --> 45:06.453
Those of you who do well today

45:07.287 --> 45:10.832
will be made full-time members
of the Ingu Sect with full benefits.

45:10.916 --> 45:12.876
- Got it?
- Yes, sir!

45:15.754 --> 45:17.172
What's this kid's problem?

45:17.255 --> 45:18.423
Hey, move over.

45:20.467 --> 45:21.468
What?

45:22.677 --> 45:23.720
Huh?

45:24.679 --> 45:25.722
Hey, you punk. Get over here.

45:26.598 --> 45:29.142
- Why?
- Get over here. Hey, grab him.

45:29.226 --> 45:30.685
Hey, get him!

45:34.648 --> 45:36.024
Get over here.

45:37.817 --> 45:38.818
Boss.

45:41.488 --> 45:43.240
Aren't you
the martial arts master's nephew?

45:43.323 --> 45:44.574
Huh?

45:44.658 --> 45:46.159
- No, I'm not.
- It is, Boss.

45:46.409 --> 45:48.828
- You've got the wrong guy.
- I know it's you.

45:49.537 --> 45:51.539
What did I tell you? I was right.

45:51.623 --> 45:53.625
The martial arts master is here.

45:54.626 --> 45:58.296
He even planted his nephew as a mole.
He really came prepared.

45:58.880 --> 46:01.007
- What should we do, Boss?
- What else?

46:02.050 --> 46:03.843
The winning hand just fell into our hands.

46:03.927 --> 46:05.345
We just gratefully accept it.

46:07.555 --> 46:10.267
You're a little adorable rat, aren't you?

46:30.745 --> 46:34.165
Man, it feels great to be
out in the field again.

46:35.417 --> 46:36.626
So what do we do now?

46:37.377 --> 46:40.005
Do we mess up
those Heaven Capital guys now?

46:41.089 --> 46:42.382
Sorry, guys.

46:42.465 --> 46:44.551
I think I'd better go alone from here.

46:44.634 --> 46:46.594
But what are you going to do on your own?

46:46.678 --> 46:49.306
What? Why?
I was hoping to finally get some action.

46:49.389 --> 46:53.518
If we move as a group out here,
we'll be way too noticeable.

46:53.601 --> 46:55.770
I'll go in alone and secure the evidence.

46:55.854 --> 46:59.024
- You can wait in the car.
- Wait, just a moment.

47:00.859 --> 47:01.860
Come on.

47:04.696 --> 47:05.739
Listen.

47:06.823 --> 47:07.991
In case anything happens

47:09.117 --> 47:10.285
use this radio.

47:10.368 --> 47:11.369
I'll come running.

47:11.453 --> 47:13.330
Thank you. I'll be right back.

47:19.085 --> 47:21.463
- We would be noticeable.
- Very.

47:29.012 --> 47:31.306
But I really think I should follow her.

47:31.389 --> 47:34.434
- She said not to.
- She's in no condition for this.

47:35.185 --> 47:38.229
She's still not fully recovered.
Someone should be with her. I'll go.

47:40.315 --> 47:41.608
Okay.

47:41.816 --> 47:43.902
- I'll be right back. Just wait here.
- Wait.

47:43.985 --> 47:45.070
Prosecutor Gang!

47:45.612 --> 47:46.738
See that?

47:46.988 --> 47:48.656
There's something going on between them.

47:59.751 --> 48:00.752
Are you okay?

48:01.586 --> 48:02.587
Yeah.

48:11.721 --> 48:14.516
- Is it all in there?
- Have I ever let you down?

48:15.433 --> 48:16.434
You can see for yourself.

48:36.246 --> 48:38.957
By the way,
why'd you call in so many people?

48:39.666 --> 48:42.836
- Is there some kind of problem?
- What problem?

48:42.919 --> 48:44.504
Let's say they're moral support.

48:44.587 --> 48:48.091
Well then, the goods are checked.

48:48.174 --> 48:49.884
And you've got your moral support.

48:50.176 --> 48:52.220
Please sign the delivery receipt.

48:58.393 --> 48:59.394
Good work.

48:59.477 --> 49:01.813
We got paid and the delivery went well.
It's a win-win.

49:01.896 --> 49:04.482
I'll let the guys in mainland know
that the deal went smoothly.

49:06.776 --> 49:08.570
I've been waiting for this day.

49:09.571 --> 49:10.905
Ah, what a beauty.

49:11.781 --> 49:13.741
Hey, let's grab it and get out of here.

49:13.825 --> 49:16.286
- Let's not waste time. Got it?
- Yes, sir.

49:18.872 --> 49:20.373
Hey, Kim. Bring it down.

49:21.541 --> 49:22.750
Yes, sir.

49:33.386 --> 49:36.181
We're all set here.
It's time to have some fun.

49:41.519 --> 49:42.520
What the hell?

49:44.230 --> 49:45.231
Go check that out.

49:46.357 --> 49:47.525
Kim, I said pull it down.

49:50.612 --> 49:52.322
Didn't you hear me? Get it down!

49:55.533 --> 49:56.576
Mr. Yoo?

49:58.119 --> 49:59.996
What's going on here?

50:03.291 --> 50:05.960
This is well within my expectations.
No need to panic.

50:08.379 --> 50:10.298
What are you waiting for?
Did you forget Plan B?

50:13.718 --> 50:16.429
All right, kids, get ready for Plan B.

50:16.513 --> 50:17.514
Let's go!

50:18.431 --> 50:19.724
- Focus. Get ready.
- Yeah.

50:24.604 --> 50:25.772
Damn it, what is that?

50:28.775 --> 50:29.901
Come on, kids.

50:29.984 --> 50:33.279
You should be holding pencils,
not weapons.

50:35.782 --> 50:37.575
Focus!

50:39.035 --> 50:40.370
- Go!
- Let's go!

50:42.914 --> 50:44.791
What the hell?

50:45.875 --> 50:47.460
Hey, are we supposed to jump?

50:49.963 --> 50:51.881
- Everyone get ready.
- Yes, sir.

50:51.965 --> 50:54.175
Boys!

51:00.056 --> 51:01.140
Look, Boss!

51:05.395 --> 51:07.063
Martial Arts Master.

51:07.146 --> 51:09.274
I was wondering when you'd show up.

51:09.357 --> 51:11.609
- Two of you this time.
- How many times do I have to say it?

51:12.360 --> 51:16.656
I said it's Masked Racer. Masked Racer!

51:18.074 --> 51:19.784
That masked freak is back.

51:20.535 --> 51:22.579
Whatever you are,
why do you keep showing up

51:22.662 --> 51:24.289
and messing with my business?

51:24.372 --> 51:28.918
Masked Racer keeps appearing
because you keep doing bad things.

51:29.752 --> 51:30.753
But today?

51:31.170 --> 51:34.591
I didn't come to mess with you.
I came to see the first snow.

51:36.467 --> 51:38.052
What is he on about?

51:40.805 --> 51:45.435
You think I'd just nod my head
and let you get away?

51:46.644 --> 51:49.856
I knew you'd be here,
so I already dug your grave, you bastard.

51:50.690 --> 51:53.318
You can't just rely on numbers
to win a fight.

51:53.401 --> 51:55.278
You have to use your head.

51:56.487 --> 51:59.824
Well, we've finally gathered
all of you good people in one place.

52:00.742 --> 52:02.160
So what do you say?

52:02.744 --> 52:04.621
Shall we watch the first snow together?

52:31.939 --> 52:33.066
What's wrong with this thing?

52:34.275 --> 52:35.818
Hey, you gotta press it harder.

52:40.782 --> 52:41.783
That's not it.

52:45.078 --> 52:46.496
Dude, it's not working.

52:46.579 --> 52:48.206
Crap, could it have gotten too old?

52:48.289 --> 52:51.084
Hey, Ho-myeong, press it harder.
Really push it.

52:52.627 --> 52:55.254
Just press it harder, you idiot!

52:57.548 --> 52:59.050
Damn it, it's not working!

52:59.550 --> 53:00.677
Is this thing broken?

53:00.760 --> 53:02.303
- What the hell?
- Damn it.

53:05.556 --> 53:07.809
- Press it harder.
- What the hell are they doing?

53:08.810 --> 53:10.728
Find out how that bastard
climbed up there.

53:12.021 --> 53:13.147
Oh, come on!

53:15.525 --> 53:16.526
Damn it!

53:58.943 --> 53:59.944
Damn it!

54:03.406 --> 54:04.574
- No!
- No.

54:04.657 --> 54:06.242
Get all those guys!

56:36.475 --> 56:38.060
I'll kill those bastards!

56:39.145 --> 56:40.980
Hey, bring me the nephew.

56:51.991 --> 56:55.119
- What are you doing here?
- Wasn't there a gunshot just now?

56:55.453 --> 56:57.496
You have no idea
how dangerous those guys are.

56:58.623 --> 57:00.374
- Stay perfectly still.
- Okay.

57:05.588 --> 57:07.965
- Did you get enough evidence?
- I am right now.

57:08.799 --> 57:10.509
This is a crucial moment.

57:14.639 --> 57:15.640
Stop!

57:16.849 --> 57:19.143
Stop unless you want to
watch this kid die!

57:19.685 --> 57:20.686
Nam-il.

57:20.978 --> 57:21.979
What did you say?

57:22.313 --> 57:23.564
My nephew, Nam-il.

57:24.148 --> 57:25.149
What's he doing there?

57:26.400 --> 57:28.110
What are you doing? Are you crazy?

57:28.235 --> 57:30.571
I have to save him.
He could die if he stays there.

57:30.655 --> 57:33.407
But what can you do? Do you have a plan?

57:33.491 --> 57:35.743
- Just wait. I'll radio it in.
- No.

57:35.826 --> 57:36.994
There's no time for that.

57:40.498 --> 57:42.625
Oh my god. What are you doing?

57:47.213 --> 57:50.341
Ms. Gang, please hit me in the head
with this as hard as you can.

57:50.424 --> 57:52.093
Are you insane?

57:55.262 --> 57:56.681
I have a plan.

57:57.348 --> 57:59.141
Just trust me.

57:59.225 --> 58:02.269
Hit me in the head as hard as you can.

58:02.395 --> 58:03.396
I'm begging you.

58:04.605 --> 58:05.606
Please.

58:05.690 --> 58:08.609
Hurry.

58:08.693 --> 58:10.820
Nam-il is going to die at this rate!

58:13.072 --> 58:14.073
Oh my god!

58:15.241 --> 58:16.283
Je-sun.

58:17.785 --> 58:19.328
This is crazy.

58:22.748 --> 58:25.167
Mi-kyung, bring the car here.
It's an emergency.

58:29.171 --> 58:30.172
Damn it.

58:30.256 --> 58:32.425
Go ahead if you want your nephew to die.

58:33.175 --> 58:34.635
Nephew? What nephew?

58:34.719 --> 58:35.761
Hey, you have a nephew?

58:35.886 --> 58:37.013
I don't have a nephew.

58:42.184 --> 58:43.894
Wait a minute. That kid.

58:44.854 --> 58:45.896
Isn't he Bulgae's nephew?

58:46.397 --> 58:47.732
Hey, don't do it!

58:47.815 --> 58:49.316
He's not one of us.

58:49.400 --> 58:52.653
You think I'll believe that?
I'm gonna slit his throat.

58:53.404 --> 58:55.406
- What the hell?
- Get those bastards!

59:26.937 --> 59:28.647
One...

59:30.066 --> 59:31.650
Two...

59:43.537 --> 59:45.039
Uncle!

01:00:13.984 --> 01:00:15.528
Screw you, scumbag gangsters!

01:00:17.530 --> 01:00:20.741
Come on! I dare you!
I'm Heo Nam-il! Got it?

01:00:20.825 --> 01:00:24.036
I'm not going down alone. I'll throw it!
I swear I'll throw it!

01:00:32.545 --> 01:00:34.839
- What happened?
- Step on it. Head that way.

01:00:34.922 --> 01:00:36.924
- Where's Bong?
- Over there.

01:00:52.481 --> 01:00:54.817
- Get in, quick!
- Hurry!

01:01:02.408 --> 01:01:03.409
We got it!

01:01:08.038 --> 01:01:09.039
Wake up!

01:01:09.790 --> 01:01:10.916
Is he hurt badly?

01:01:11.208 --> 01:01:13.002
I don't know.
I don't see any external injuries.

01:01:14.503 --> 01:01:17.214
- His breathing's normal too.
- He turned into the Hulk.

01:01:17.298 --> 01:01:18.382
The Hulk?

01:01:19.341 --> 01:01:20.885
He'll be fine in a little bit.

01:01:22.261 --> 01:01:23.721
My uncle's no ordinary person.

01:01:23.804 --> 01:01:26.515
Forget about that!
Why was he on the ground over there?

01:01:26.932 --> 01:01:28.225
Ah, Prosecutor Gang!

01:01:28.309 --> 01:01:30.561
You got the video you wanted, right?

01:01:30.895 --> 01:01:33.147
I did, but there were some complications.

01:01:33.230 --> 01:01:36.108
- Complications?
- Let's just get back. I'll tell you then.

01:01:48.829 --> 01:01:50.956
- Should we go?
- Yeah. You okay?

01:01:51.040 --> 01:01:52.041
Yeah.

01:01:53.542 --> 01:01:54.543
What is it?

01:01:56.128 --> 01:01:57.129
I recognize that car.

01:01:57.213 --> 01:01:59.965
- Whatever. Just go.
- Okay.

01:02:09.934 --> 01:02:12.019
- We're done here. Let's get out.
- Huh?

01:02:12.561 --> 01:02:13.729
- Hey, it's time.
- Let's go!

01:02:24.281 --> 01:02:26.325
Hey, Boss, wake up already!

01:02:28.661 --> 01:02:30.537
Go after them, you idiots!

01:02:32.331 --> 01:02:33.874
Those bastards! Damn it!

01:02:43.384 --> 01:02:45.052
Unbelievable.

01:02:46.679 --> 01:02:47.680
Let's go.

01:02:51.058 --> 01:02:53.686
- Go after them!
- What's wrong with this thing?

01:02:53.769 --> 01:02:55.938
- What now?
- Something's wrong with the car.

01:02:56.021 --> 01:02:58.023
- Why isn't it working?
- Damn it!

01:03:00.818 --> 01:03:02.194
YEONGSEON FOOD

01:03:08.909 --> 01:03:09.910
Hurry up, you idiot!

01:03:11.829 --> 01:03:12.830
Come on!

01:03:20.921 --> 01:03:22.631
Yeah!

01:03:27.803 --> 01:03:29.596
That was freaking rough!

01:03:41.692 --> 01:03:44.320
SPECIAL THANKS TO
KIM SANG-KYUNG AND KWON YUL

01:03:59.126 --> 01:04:02.463
So these so-called Masked Racers
suddenly appeared out of nowhere

01:04:02.588 --> 01:04:04.381
and blew up all the drugs?

01:04:04.465 --> 01:04:06.592
- Hey, Boss!
- A double agent?

01:04:06.675 --> 01:04:09.553
- You sure you can handle this?
- Patrolling is my specialty. Don't worry.

01:04:09.636 --> 01:04:12.097
Honestly, she seemed
very suspicious to me.

01:04:12.222 --> 01:04:14.350
So she approached
Gang Beom-ryong on purpose?

01:04:14.433 --> 01:04:15.768
I'll watch him closely.

01:04:15.851 --> 01:04:18.103
You think I'm stupid enough
to let something like this break me?

01:04:20.022 --> 01:04:21.565
Je-sun. I'm just asking.

01:04:21.648 --> 01:04:24.610
What would you do if your past self
was a completely different person?

01:04:24.693 --> 01:04:26.236
You turned into the Hulk yesterday.

01:04:26.320 --> 01:04:27.571
Jeong Ho-myeong and I

01:04:27.654 --> 01:04:29.198
could be back at each other's throats
at any moment.

01:04:29.281 --> 01:04:31.950
- You bastard.
- You're the only one I can count on.

01:04:32.076 --> 01:04:35.496
- It's not too late for you to pull out.
- Is this a threat?

01:04:35.579 --> 01:04:38.207
- Gather all of our boys.
- You have to take responsibility.

01:04:38.290 --> 01:04:40.793
- I'm already prepared.
- Where the hell did Bulgae come from?

01:04:40.918 --> 01:04:43.796
- It was Je-sun.
- This is no coincidence.

01:04:43.879 --> 01:04:45.339
Change of plans.
